      "writtenOn": "2021-10-21T14:01:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was trying to come up with a clever way to make this little struct more opaque to the draws themselves and only the CommandBuffer class would actually be able to extract the real buffer and offset from them. However, we would still need a way for higher up code to at least know if they have the same buffer \"id\" or not. This can all be done with make things private and friending certain things and having a public \"void* getID() { return fBuffer; }. Additionally draws will need to know their offset into the vertex/index buffer since these are typically params passed into the draw itself and not the bind.\n\nBut a lot of this seems like overkill just to make sure the draws don\u0027t try to access to buffer themselves. What do you all think here. I\u0027m open to any suggestions.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 153,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 156,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "4fa6cbed509fe3a07caa66b3029f33cadc5e5287",
