    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "335e3e4d_2e2b7353",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/DrawBufferManager.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 28,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-21T14:01:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I am trying to avoid the CommandBuffers having to take lots of extra refs on the same buffers. Like we could instead take refs during bindBuffer calls. This probably is okay for vertex/index calls since we generally bind a buffer once at offset 0, and then the draw calls themselves offset into the buffer. So there would only be 1 call to bind per buffer and thus only one ref taken. Currently how things are setup (in Ganesh) for uniforms we would end up binding the uniform multiple times at different offsets because all the shaders offset their uniforms relative to a buffer logically starting at 0.\n\nSo using this approach just makes all the buffers go through the same system, but does have the side effects of being uglier and requiring a public call on CommandBuffer just to pass in refs.",
      "range": {
